---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
const lastUpdated = "July 31, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={`${siteConfig.name}'s privacy policy: what data is collected, how it's used, and which third-party services are involved.`}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} is a small, independently-run technical blog. This policy
      explains what happens when you read it.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site collects today</h2>
    <p>
      As of this writing, {siteConfig.name} does not run any analytics, tracking pixels,
      or advertising scripts, and does not set cookies for visitors. Reading the site
      does not create an account, a session, or any stored profile of you. Server
      logs at the hosting layer (Cloudflare) may record standard technical data —
      IP address, user agent, requested URL, timestamp — the same way any web server
      does;
      {siteConfig.name} does not access or process these logs beyond normal operational
      troubleshooting.
    </p>

    <h2>What may be added later, and how it will be handled</h2>
    <p>
      If {siteConfig.name} adds Cloudflare Web Analytics, it is a cookieless, IP-anonymizing
      analytics product — it does not use client-side identifiers or cross-site tracking.
      If comments are added (via Giscus, which authenticates through your own GitHub
      account), that exchange happens directly between you and GitHub; {
        siteConfig.name
      }
      does not see or store your GitHub credentials. If advertising, affiliate links,
      or a newsletter are ever added, this page will be updated first, and any tracking
      that requires consent (for example Google Analytics) will be gated behind an
      actual consent prompt, not just a mention on this page. See the{" "}
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate/Advertising Disclosure</a>{" "}
      page for the current status of monetization on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      Posts on {siteConfig.name} link out to external tools, documentation, and services.
      Once you follow an outbound link, that site's own privacy practices apply —
      this policy only covers {siteConfig.name}{" "}
      itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Because no personal data is currently collected or stored by this site,
      there is nothing to request deletion of today. If that changes, this page
      will describe exactly what's collected and how to request its removal. In
      the meantime, if you have a privacy question, reach out via the <a
        href="/contact/">Contact</a
      > page.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This page will be updated whenever what {siteConfig.name} collects or how it's
      handled changes — the "Last updated" date above reflects the most recent revision.
    </p>

    <p class="legal__disclaimer">
      This page is provided for transparency and is not a substitute for legal
      advice.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .legal__updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * -2);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 6);
  }

  .legal__disclaimer {
    margin-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 8);
    padding-top: calc(var(--spacing) * 4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
</style>
